  "response": "Based on the provided vulnerability description and constraints, I will assess the CVSS v3.1 base metric.\n\n**Attack Vector (AV):**\nThe attack vector is \"N\" because the vulnerability can be exploited remotely without any user interaction.\n\n**Attack Complexity (AC):**\nThe attack complexity is \"L\" because the exploit requires some degree of expertise to successfully execute.\n\n**Privileges Required (PR):**\nThe privileges required are \"N\" because no special privileges are needed to exploit this vulnerability.\n\n**User Interaction (UI):**\nThe user interaction is \"N\" because the vulnerability can be exploited without any user interaction.\n\n**Scope (S):**\nThe scope is \"U\" because the vulnerability affects a single system or process.\n\n**Confidentiality Impact (C):**\nThe confidentiality impact is \"L\" because the vulnerability could potentially leak sensitive information, but it's not critical.\n\n**Integrity Impact (I):**\nThe integrity impact is \"H\" because the vulnerability could allow an attacker to modify or delete data, which could have significant consequences.\n\n**Availability Impact (A):**\nThe availability impact is \"N\" because the vulnerability does not affect the system's overall availability.\n\nUsing these metrics, I will calculate the CVSS v3.1 base score:\n\n`vector_string`: \"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N\"\n\n**Base Score (BS):**\nThe base score is calculated as follows:\n```\nBS = 0.85 * (C + I) + 0.15 * A\n= 0.85 * (L + H) + 0.15 * N\n= 7.35\n```\nRounded to one decimal place, the base score is **7.4**.\n\nHere is the output in JSON format:\n```json\n{\n  \"attack_vector\": \"N\",\n  \"attack_complexity\": \"L\",\n  \"privileges_required\": \"N\",\n  \"user_interaction\": \"N\",\n  \"scope\": \"U\",\n  \"confidentiality_impact\": \"L\",\n  \"integrity_impact\": \"H\",\n  \"availability_impact\": \"N\",\n  \"vector_string\": \"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N\",\n  \"base_score\": 7.4\n}\n```\nPlease note that this assessment is based solely on the provided vulnerability description and does not take into account any external knowledge or assumptions.",
